@startuml
title P3 E2EE Media Rotation, History Grant, and Report Evidence
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Sender A" as A
participant "Sender Pulsar" as Sender
participant "Coordinator" as Coord
participant "Recipient C" as C
participant "Revoked B" as B
participant "New Device D" as D
participant "Moderator" as Mod

== Protected send ==
A -> Sender : choose media + audience
Sender -> Sender : normalize / encode locally
Sender -> Sender : encrypt media\nwrap key to current epoch recipients
Sender -> Coord : upload ciphertext + manifest + recipient wraps
Coord -> Coord : store opaque objects\nseal transmission to target snapshot + epoch
Coord -> C : deliver manifest + ciphertext refs
C -> C : unwrap key, verify epoch,\ndecrypt and play locally

== Membership revoke and rotation ==
Coord -> Coord : revoke B or remove B from Air
Coord -> Coord : rotate to next epoch\nfor remaining members
Coord --> B : no new wraps or epoch grants
B -> Coord : fetch fresh protected media
Coord --> B : deny manifest or key access

== New device without history ==
D -> Coord : join or recover installation
Coord --> D : current epoch bootstrap only
D -> Coord : request older protected media
Coord --> D : denied until explicit history grant
A -> Coord : approve history grant for D
Coord --> D : time-bound grant for approved history range
D -> D : import grant and decrypt\napproved old media only

== Voluntary report evidence ==
C -> C : choose Report
alt Recipient exports decrypted evidence
  C -> C : confirm explicit evidence copy
  C -> Coord : report metadata + provided evidence package
  Coord -> Mod : expose audit + provided copy
else Metadata-only report
  C -> Coord : report metadata without decrypted copy
  Coord -> Mod : expose metadata only
end
Mod -> Coord : take moderation action

note over Coord
Coordinator stores manifests, ciphertext,
wrapped keys, and audit metadata.
It never performs hidden server decryption.
end note
@enduml
